    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3005" root="بقع" body-key="b">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقّع الثَّوْبَ</span></b>  <i>He</i> (a dyer) <i>left spots,</i> or <i>portions, of the garment,</i> or <i>piece of cloth, undyed.</i>
(Mgh, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقّع ثَوْبَهُ</span> <i>He</i> (a waterer) <i>sprinkled
the water upon his garment, so that spots,</i> or
<i>portions, of it became wetted.</i> (Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقّع</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَطَرُ فِى مَوَاضِعَ مِنَ الأَرْضِ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَبْقِيعٌ</span>, <i>The
rain fell in places of the land, not universally.</i>
(TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَدْرِى أَيْنَ بَقَّعَ</span>: see 1.

